  "interpretation": "This compact table-summary cross-check retains no full tap-power table. Tap count means resolved delay clusters. For LOS TDL-D, the specular and diffuse first components share the zero-delay cluster; the specular component is not an additional delay. The check can detect cluster-count, delay-span, and lattice-resolution mismatches, but it does not verify each tap power, fading distribution, LOS K-factor, or statistical behavior."
